# nsMsgProgress::GetMsgWindow behavior in mailnews/base/src/nsMsgProgress.cpp

Rejects null output pointer. If a weak-reference object exists it queries the referent; otherwise writes null. It ignores the referent query's nsresult and always returns NS_OK afterward, so callers cannot use its success result alone to infer a live window.

## State read

- m_msgWindow

## State changed

- aMsgWindow output through QueryReferent, or null when no weak reference

## Calls and triggers

- Firefox CallQueryReferent delegates to nsIWeakReference::QueryReferent atxpcom/base/nsIWeakReferenceUtils.h:22-27.

## Result and consumers

NS_OK after lookup; returned interface may be unavailable. Exact failed-query output behavior depends on referent implementation.

## Errors

Null output pointer rejected; QueryReferent failure suppressed.

## Async completion

Synchronous lookup.

## Ownership and cleanup

Successful queried interface is an owning output reference under QueryReferent contract; not a persistent strong field.

